  "conclusion": "Full sample (2005-2026): Best VIX-DCA = Binary VIX>20 ($1,294,246 vs Plain $1,095,200, +18.2%). No VIX-DCA variant achieved statistical significance (p<0.05) over Plain DCA. Cross-OOS: Fear DCA most consistent (3/3 periods beat Plain DCA). OOS wins: {'Fear DCA': 3, 'Proportional VIX': 3, 'Percentile VIX': 2, 'Binary VIX>20': 3}. Average cost advantage: Binary VIX>20 avg cost $126.11 vs Plain $149.03 (+15.4%). Lump Sum (invest all day 1) terminal: $2,041,920 (+86.4% vs Plain DCA). Key finding: VIX-timed DCA mechanically buys more shares when prices are lower (VIX-price negative correlation), achieving a lower average cost per share. The improvement is modest but systematic.",
